ool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.006844292668247904,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":18.7,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.23794001,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Brookfield Wealth Solutions Ltd., through its subsidiaries, provides retirement services, wealth protection products, and capital solutions to individuals and institutions. It operates through Annuities, Property and Casualty (P&C), Life Insurance segments. The Annuities segment offers retail and institutional annuities, including fixed index, fixed rate, single premium immediate, and variable annuities, as well as pension risk transfer. The P&C segment provides specialty casualty, construction defect, general liability, commercial multi-peril, workers compensation, product and environmental liability, and auto liability. The Life Insurance segment offers whole life, universal life, and variable universal life insurance products. It also offers garage and inland marine insurance programs. The company was formerly known as Brookfield Reinsurance Ltd. and changed its name to Brookfield Wealth Solutions Ltd. in September 2024. Brookfield Wealth Solutions Ltd. was incorporated in 2020 and is headquartered in Pembroke, Bermuda.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sachin G. Shah C.P.A. | CEO, Head of Insurance Solutions Business & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $2.9M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 29%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $636K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Brookfield Wealth Solutions Ltd is a large-cap financial services business with a $11.2B market cap on $11.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +29% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 29% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 18-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $2.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.03\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 24% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.8pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 59% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5890074605722919},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 76% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Brookfield Wealth Solutions (BNT) Could Be 26% Overvalued After Annuity Growth And Just Group Deal","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-bnt/brookfield-wealth-solutions/news/brookfield-wealth-solutions-bnt-could-be-26-overvalued-after","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794172656.865,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.986,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why (BNT) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.